{
  "_readme": [
    "AGARTALA / TRIPURA TEMPLATE — fill this in and save it as doctors.json",
    "",
    "One blank entry per speciality, so nothing the triage can recommend ends in",
    "a dead end. Duplicate an entry to add a second doctor for that speciality.",
    "",
    "ONLY 'name' and 'specialty' are required. Delete any line you cannot fill —",
    "a missing field just leaves that row off the card. Do NOT leave the",
    "placeholder text in: 'Dr. ' with nothing after it will be skipped, and",
    "'+91 00000 00000' would show a patient a number that does not ring.",
    "",
    "HOURS: each day is a LIST of intervals, so a clinic with separate morning",
    "and evening sittings is two pairs. [] or a missing day means closed.",
    "Use {\"always_open\": true} for a 24-hour emergency department.",
    "",
    "LAT/LNG: right-click the clinic in Google Maps and copy the two numbers.",
    "Both or neither. Agartala sits at roughly 23.83 N, 91.28 E, so a correct",
    "entry looks like \"lat\": 23.83xx, \"lng\": 91.27xx. If your longitude comes",
    "out near 23 you have them the wrong way round.",
    "",
    "LANGUAGES: Bengali and Kokborok are both official languages of Tripura.",
    "Listing which a doctor actually speaks is one of the more useful things in",
    "this file, and something no hospital website tells you.",
    "",
    "VERIFY EVERY NUMBER BY CALLING IT before anyone else uses this app. A wrong",
    "number in a triage app is worse than no number at all."
  ],

